<newsitem itemid="442222" id="root" date="1997-03-14" xml:lang="en">
<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Bowler Metcalf raises yr share, div.</title>
<headline>Bowler Metcalf raises yr share, div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     8.2	   vs 6.9</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 2.9	   vs 2.5</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   6.95	  vs 5.84</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		  10.36	  vs 8.43</p>
<p>    Tax			 3.41	  vs 2.59</p>
<p>    Turnover		 46.66	  vs 39.88</p>
<p>Payable on register April 4</p>
<p>Full name: Bowler Metcalf Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - The directors proposed that a dividend of 1.7 cents per share be payable to shareholders. They said the company has invested a further 4.0 million rand in new PET equipment since the year end to broaden its product range in line with international trends. They said the benefits should be felt this year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
